+### Retries and source locations (4.2.0)
+
+Three optional fields, the ones a runner knows and the report model always had room for:
+
+| Field | On | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `attempt` | `start` (and optionally `end`, `step`, `assertion`) | Which run of the test this is, 1-based: 1 for the first run, 2 for the first retry, as the runner's own retries count it within one run (Jest's `retryTimes`, Playwright's `retries`). → `Scenario.Attempt`, which history reads as "passed on retry N" (Flaky) and CTRF as `retries`. A record other than a `start` that carries it belongs to that attempt, whatever its timestamp. |
+| `sourceFile` | `start` | The file the test is written in → `Scenario.SourceFile` (`Failures.md`'s "written at", CTRF's `filePath`, `kronikol query failures`), and the feature's source file when it has none yet (the first one seen wins). |
+| `sourceFile` | `step`, `assertion` | The call site's file → the step's `SourceFile`, of which the report keeps the file name (the step contract): `Failures.md` prints it beside a failing step. |
+| `sourceLine` | `start`, `step`, `assertion` | The test's declaration line, or the call site's line. 1-based. |
+
+**Retries.** Keep one `testId` per test across its retries, as the runners do, and write a `start` per attempt.
+The report shows the **last attempt**, the rule the [Cucumber Messages](#cucumber-messages) lane has always
+had: its verdict, error, duration, steps and attachments, `Scenario.Attempt` set, and a `retry N` label for
+each earlier attempt (N being that attempt's number). The earlier attempts' calls, every call of the test made
+before its last attempt started, are left out, and one diagnostic counts them. A second `start` without
+`attempt` is read as the next attempt, and a diagnostic says how many tests were read that way. Before 4.2.0 a
+retried test was one scenario holding both attempts' steps and calls, which kept the failed attempt's error
+under a passed verdict; a producer that gave each attempt its own `testId` got two scenarios, one failed, and a
+run that read as failed although the retry passed. Two ids for one test are still two scenarios: write one.
+
+**Paths.** `\` and `/` are both accepted, and a leading `./` or a `file://` scheme is dropped. An absolute path
+under `--source-root` (`IngestRequest.SourceRoot`; default: the directory the command runs in, which in CI is
+the checkout) is written relative to it. One outside it is kept as written, and a diagnostic counts them: a
+build machine's paths do not belong in a downloadable report. The root is a prefix, not a directory the
+ingesting machine must have, so a Windows runner's `D:\a\repo\repo` can be named on Linux.
+
+```json
+{"event":"start","testId":"…","testName":"charges a card","feature":"charge","sourceFile":"src/charge.test.ts","sourceLine":12,"attempt":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-30T10:00:03Z"}
+{"event":"step","testId":"…","text":"the card is charged","status":"failed","error":"expected 201, received 502","sourceFile":"src/charge.test.ts","sourceLine":18,"timestamp":"2026-09-30T10:00:04Z"}
+```
+
 ### Attachments (`event: "attachment"`)
 
 Screenshots, traces, videos and links a runner produced, carried into the report as scenario- or
@@ -225,6 +261,7 @@ kronikol ingest ./captures --tests ./captures/tests.ndjson -o ./Reports -t "E2E
 | `--phase-from-steps` | off | Give interactions the phase of the `Given`/`When`/`Then` step they happened during: each call's `phase` in the data files and for `kronikol query`. It draws nothing; the Setup partition is `--separate-setup`'s (before 4.1.0 this row said otherwise, and it never drew one) — see [Phases from steps](#phases-from-steps). |
 | `--separate-setup` | off | Draw each test's setup calls inside a `Setup` partition, as an in-process run with `SeparateSetup` does: the calls before its first `When`/`Then` step that follows a `Given` step, else before its first call phased `Action` that follows one phased `Setup`. A capture's own boundary wins. Sets `ReportConfigurationOptions.SeparateSetup` (4.1.0+) — see [The Setup partition](#the-setup-partition-410). |
 | `--attachments-base <dir>` | cwd | Resolve relative `attachment` paths against this directory. |
+| `--source-root <dir>` | cwd | Write a tests record's absolute `sourceFile` relative to this directory; one outside it is kept and counted (4.2.0+) — see [Retries and source locations](#retries-and-source-locations-420). |
 | `--clean-attachments` | off | Empty the report's `attachments/` folder first, so it holds exactly this run's artefacts. |
 | `--cucumber-messages <file>` | — | A Cucumber Messages NDJSON (repeatable) — the Gherkin structure of a BDD run. Wins over `--tests` for the scenarios it owns; see [Cucumber Messages](#cucumber-messages). |
 | `--include-hooks` | off | Keep the Cucumber hook steps (`BeforeEach hook`, …) in the step list. |
